# Grid distance & pathfinding

**Default:** all range checks and movement paths use **Chebyshev** distance (8-directional — diagonals count as 1 tile), unless a feature explicitly opts out.

- Distance: `GridMath.chebyshev(a, b)` — `max(|dx|, |dy|)`
- Neighbors / BFS steps: `GridMath.chebyshev_neighbors(pos)`
- Attack range, move reachability, and `PathfindingSystem` paths all follow this
- Prefer Chebyshev over Manhattan for new combat/movement logic

**Opt-out only when specified** (e.g. an ability that must be orthogonal-only). Then use `GridMath.manhattan` / `GridMath.orthogonal_neighbors` and document why on that ability.
